{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender non modal operator blender non modal operator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","fileName":"Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Non-Modal Operator","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Operator and Event System]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Exec Callback","Blender Operator Poll Method","Blender Operator Handler Dispatch","Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender non modal operator blender non modal operator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","fileName":"Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Non-Modal Operator","heading":"Blender Non-Modal Operator","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A non-modal Blender operator completes its action in one callback rather than remaining active across a sequence of user events. Its type can often be defined with only an [[Blender Operator Exec Callback]] and the [[Blender Operator Poll Method]] that validates the context.\n\nThe Outliner select-all example and the custom editor's color buttons follow this form. After [[Blender Operator Handler Dispatch]] locates the registered type, polling checks availability, execution updates data, and the call returns an operator status without entering a [[Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Exec Callback","Blender Operator Poll Method","Blender Operator Handler Dispatch","Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender non modal operator blender non modal operator","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","fileName":"Blender Non-Modal Operator.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Non-Modal Operator","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[coreblenderdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Operator and Event System","Blender Operator Exec Callback","Blender Operator Poll Method","Blender Operator Handler Dispatch","Blender Modal Operator Lifecycle","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}